  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Blame It On The Weather** (1 other source): This performance marked the first live appearance of the song, following its introduction two days earlier [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Blame It On The Weather**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 12 archived performances [5]\n- **Mystery Jack**: back after 57 archived shows (3036 days); rare: 4 archived performances [5]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Magenta Mountain, Gaia, The Garden Goblin, The Dripping Tap [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **kglw2022-03-07** (recommended): source not stated; 14 songs; 95 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: The FLAC files contain no audio content and fail to play in Audacity [3]\n- **KGLW_2022-03-07**: source not stated; 1 songs; 97 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The floor was wobbly from a previous collapse, and the venue was hot and crowded [4]\n- Many attendees and band members contracted COVID, forcing the cancellation of the South American tour leg [4]\n- The venue floor had just collapsed in a city currently at risk of flooding [1]\n- The set concluded with a jam session lasting over twenty minutes, energizing the enraptured crowd [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **kglw2022-03-07**: taped by philandjenny; transferred by MaxEgg; source: Audacity > CDWav > TLH [1]\n- **KGLW_2022-03-07**: taped by philandjenny; source: Sony PCM 10 [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by KGLW.net: [King Gizzard & the Lizard Wizard setlist - 2022-03-07 Enmore Theatre, Warrane (Sydney), NSW, Australia](https://kglw.net/setlists/king-gizzard-the-lizard-wizard-march-7-2022-enmore-theatre-eora-sydney-nsw-australia.html) [6]",
